## QuantiveCorp.Framework.Middleman 

This project is an implementation of the mediator pattern.

# Configure in Program.cs

```csharp
using sge.framework.middleman
builder.Services.AddMiddlemanConfig();
```

# Usage

1. Create a command class that implements `IMiddlemanRequest<TResponse>` and a handler class that implements `IMiddlemanRequestHandler<TRequest, TResponse>`.
```csharp
using sge.framework.middleman;

public class MyCommand : IMiddlemanRequest<TResponse>
{
    // Properties
}
```
2. Create a handler class that implements `IMiddlemanRequestHandler<TRequest, TResponse>`.

```csharp
public class MyCommandHandler : IMiddlemanRequestHandler<MyCommand, TResponse>
{
    public Task<TResponse> Handle(MyCommand request, CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        // Handle the command
    }
}
```

3. Call the command from your controller or service using the `IMediator` interface.
```csharp
using sge.framework.middleman;

public class YourController : ControllerBase
{
    private readonly IMiddlemanSender middlemanSender;

    public YourController(IMiddlemanSender middlemanSender)
    {
        this.middlemanSender = middlemanSender;
    }

    [HttpPost]
    public async Task<IActionResult> Create([FromBody] MyCommand command)
    {
        var response = await middlemanSender.Send(command);
        return Ok(response);
    }
}
```

